{"name":"Peach Melba","hex":"#fbbdaf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Peach Melba","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A classic French dessert, made from peaches and raspberry sauce accompanied with vanilla ice cream."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Peach_Melba"}],"entries":[{"title":"Peach Melba","blocks":[{"text":"Peach Melba is a dessert of peaches and raspberry sauce with vanilla ice cream. It was invented in 1892 or 1893 by the French chef Auguste Escoffier at the Savoy Hotel, London, to honour the Australian soprano Nellie Melba."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Peach_Melba.jpg/330px-Peach_Melba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach_Melba","wikidata":"Q1567954"},{"title":"Peach Melba (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Peach Melba is the fourth album by singer Melba Moore, released in 1975: her Buddah Records debut, Peach Melba was Moore's first studio album since 1971. Moore would credit her husband/manager Charles Huggins, whom she married in September 1974, with getting her signed to Buddah."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/40/MelbaMoore_Peach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach_Melba_(album)","wikidata":"Q7157643"},{"title":"Peach","blocks":[{"text":"The peach is a deciduous tree that bears edible juicy fruits with various characteristics. Most are simply called peaches, while the glossy-skinned, non-fuzzy varieties are called nectarines. Though from the same species, they are regarded commercially as different fruits."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg/330px-Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach","wikidata":"Q13189"},{"title":"Peach (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Peach is a color that is named for the pale color of the interior flesh of the peach fruit. Like the color apricot, the color peach is paler than most actual peach fruits and seems to have been formulated primarily to create a pastel palette of colors for interior design."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach_(color)","wikidata":"Q5148721"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Autumn_Red_peaches.jpg/500px-Autumn_Red_peaches.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Autumn_Red_peaches.jpg/1280px-Autumn_Red_peaches.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Autumn_Red_peaches.jpg/500px-Autumn_Red_peaches.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAutumn_Red_peaches.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Peachblossoms3800ppx.JPG/250px-Peachblossoms3800ppx.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Peachblossoms3800ppx.JPG/330px-Peachblossoms3800ppx.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Peachblossoms3800ppx.JPG/250px-Peachblossoms3800ppx.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APeachblossoms3800ppx.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Prunus_persica%EF%BC%88%E8%8A%B1%E6%A1%83%EF%BC%894035837.JPG/250px-Prunus_persica%EF%BC%88%E8%8A%B1%E6%A1%83%EF%BC%894035837.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn